<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2">
  <Document>
    <name>🌤️ LIVE VISIBILITY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<p><b>Legend</b><br><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/visibility/legend.png" width="600" alt="legend"><br>Meteorological visibility in statute miles (HRRR surface analysis, FAA flight-category scale): <b>0-0.25 Dense fog</b> maroon (NWS Dense Fog Advisory, 1/4 mi or less) &rarr; <b>0.25-1 LIFR</b> red &rarr; <b>1-3 IFR</b> orange &rarr; <b>3-5 MVFR</b> gold &rarr; <b>5-30 VFR</b> green to deep blue (10SM is the METAR reporting cap; the model resolves past it). Same visibility always shows the same color; above 30 mi clamps into deep blue. Human-observer/mariner/pilot visibility through haze, mist, precipitation, and smoke — not astronomical seeing.</p><p>This entry auto-refreshes from the live overlay (source: NOAA/NCEP HRRR 3 km surface visibility analysis, hourly cycles).</p><p>Turn on/off independently of all other layers. Add this file once; new source cycles appear automatically.</p><p><i>Not endorsed by NOAA.</i></p>]]></description>
    <NetworkLink>
      <name>🌤️ LIVE VISIBILITY — auto-refresh</name>
      <Link>
        <href>https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/kml/live/Great_Lakes_Live_Atmospheric_Visibility.kml</href>
        <refreshMode>onInterval</refreshMode>
        <refreshInterval>3600</refreshInterval>
      </Link>
    </NetworkLink>
  </Document>
</kml>
